  ],
  "description": "STELLA (InfraSTructurEs for Living LAbs) is a DFG-funded collaboration between TH Köln, GESIS, and ZB MED that provides an integrated e-research environment for evaluating search and recommender systems with real users in productive web-based academic search portals—going beyond offline TREC studies and laboratory-only user experiments. STELLA I (2018–2022) established the living-lab infrastructure, connected LIVIVO via API, integrated recommender systems, and supported the CLEF LiLAS evaluation lab. STELLA II (2023–2026, DFG 407518790) extends the framework to partners DIPF, TIB, and ZBW, adds continuous evaluation, and consolidates Docker infrastructure, common indexing, rich logging, expert test collections, and sustainability planning. At ZB MED, the Semantic Technologies team leads project management, portal integration, test-collection creation, and research on document-to-document relevance assessment and ranking methodology for life-science search.",
